1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa River

2
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:24,660
When I kick a pebble, even my shoes fly off

3
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:32,980
I wonder if I should be saving up my money

4
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:39,120
They laughed at me for still being a kid

5
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I leave my energy somewhere

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,300
Nothing changes, not even one yawn

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,180
The streets somehow feel so gentle

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,180
From the pointed hat, from the water flask

9
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:07,440
The sunset falls into the vast sky

10
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end this way too, won't it

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,720
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness again, they say

12
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:22,440
After running all around, I realized

13
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:24,680
Because I'm such a fool

14
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:31,500
The human crane of desire

15
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,220
I wonder what's wrong with the Chief.

16
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:44,500
He's been sighing all morning.

17
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:46,000
Well, you see,

18
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,320
I hear he had a fight with Hiromi.

19
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:50,140
Really?

20
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:52,960
He's the apple of his eye,

21
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:56,380
and apparently he isn't even
allowed to see his grandson Daisuke.

22
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:58,920
Chief, where are you headed?

23
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:01,260
I'm just going out on patrol for a bit.

24
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,780
Mind the station while I'm gone.

25
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:03,520
Yes!

26
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,340
He seems to be taking it pretty hard,
doesn't he.

27
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:09,640
Yeah, he does.

28
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,680
Wow!

29
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:15,360
Three at once!

30
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:16,660
I wonder why he came.

31
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:17,660
No way!

32
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,040
I'll give these to you guys.

33
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:22,160
Yay!

34
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:24,820
Nobody can beat Ryo-san at video games, but

35
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:26,880
he's a genius at crane games too.

36
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:27,400
Yeah.

37
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:31,300
Let me teach you the tricks of the crane game,
just for you.

38
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:32,180
Hey, Ryotsu!

39
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:34,100
What do you think you're doing on duty?

40
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:35,080
Chief!

41
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,240
Well, you see...

42
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:38,600
It's not like I was slacking
off on the job or anything.

43
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:40,040
Local resident

44
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:42,040
Crane shop owner

45
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:43,040
How's that?

46
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:44,860
Didn't I look just like the Chief?

47
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:46,840
Don't scare me like that!

48
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:49,260
That's unusual, coming from you.

49
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:52,720
Not even joining the shopping district event,
and you're just hanging around here?

50
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,620
Event? What's that?

51
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:56,120
You don't know?

52
00:02:56,360 --> 00:03:00,740
It's where people act as the
cranes to grab super luxury prizes.

53
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:01,820
Really?

54
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:05,600
We'd better hurry,
or registration will be closing soon.

55
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:09,060
Oh no, they've already left.

56
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:12,420
Grab the luxury prizes!

57
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:17,660
We did it, Ashimoto Sakaguchi Gumi!

58
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:20,000
We're in first place for total prize value.

59
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:22,300
Damn, it's a two-person team?

60
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:27,940
You there.

61
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:30,440
Won't you join me as a
crane in the crane game?

62
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:32,860
Don't run away like that!

63
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:36,240
You there, with me...

64
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,340
Gorilla.

65
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:37,520
Oh my!

66
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:38,700
Damn it!

67
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,920
You there, the beautiful long-haired lady!

68
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:46,440
Whoa!

69
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:49,160
Watch out, watch out!

70
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:54,940
How about you? Be a human crane with me...

71
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:55,800
Chief!

72
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:02,180
That's strange. Usually around this time,

73
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:04,600
Idiot! What do you think
you're doing during work hours?

74
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:07,340
it should be happening, but...

75
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:11,940
Something's off.

76
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:15,700
I hope it's not a sign of Denpechī.

77
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:17,800
That Chief...

78
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:20,000
What's wrong?

79
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,440
You look like you've been
fighting with Hiromi or something.

80
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,800
How do you know about that too?

81
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:29,220
Are you two really fighting?

82
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:32,780
It's not really a fight or anything.

83
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:38,680
he was just shut out, and even when I visited the house,
they wouldn't let me see Daisuke's face.

84
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:50,200
That's quite the fight! What caused it? I think it was when I visited
Hiromi's house the other day and spilled tea on an idol's autographed card.

85
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:53,000
What's the idol's name?

86
00:04:53,680 --> 00:05:00,760
I think it was a group called Smappi.
Smappi? You know about them? Of course I do!

87
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:08,500
Listen, SMAP is the biggest idol group right now.
99.999% of all Japanese people know them.

88
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:13,660
They're the most famous idol group in Japan,
loved by people of all ages and genders.

89
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:15,840
Only the Chief doesn't know them.

90
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:17,534
I-is that so?

91
00:05:17,584 --> 00:05:20,820
So that's why Hiromi was so angry.

92
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,480
I see, so that's why they'd
be prizes at this event.

93
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:28,140
Smappy's autographed card

94
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:32,160
The Kameari Shopping District
Association is not to be underestimated.

95
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:34,400
Time is running short now.

96
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:37,480
I'd like to make the next
participant the last one.

97
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:40,820
Does anyone want to participate?

98
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,660
Let's join, Chief!

99
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:43,640
W-What?

100
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,080
We're going to be the
cranes in the crane game.

101
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:47,900
This is your chance to make up with Hiromi.

102
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:49,420
W-What did you say?

103
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:51,880
That Smappy autographed
card over there is also fate.

104
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:56,120
Heaven is telling you to win
that card and give it to Hiromi.

105
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:58,500
But, you know,

106
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:02,360
Well, I feel bad about skipping work too,

107
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:04,580
but if we let this chance slip by,

108
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:07,380
you may never make up with
Hiromi for the rest of your life!

109
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:09,400
Don't be so dramatic.

110
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:11,560
You're naive, you know.

111
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:15,360
Parent-child relationships fall
apart over the smallest things.

112
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:20,960
I know a father and daughter who
haven't spoken to each other in 20 years,

113
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:23,120
and you'll never guess what started it.

114
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,060
The father's fart stank too much.

115
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:29,680
To restore a harmonious
parent-child relationship,

116
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,880
we have no choice but to seize this chance.

117
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:33,320
This Ryotsu Kankichi,

118
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:35,520
I'll lend you a hand,
though it's a humble effort.

119
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:39,000
But if someone sees us, it'll be a problem.

120
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:42,040
Come on, is there no other
brave challenger out there?

121
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:45,620
If we don't hurry,
someone else will take the spot!

122
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:48,580
Hey!

123
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:50,380
Ryotsu!

124
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,740
And now,
the final challenger takes the stage!

125
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:03,820
Your name is...

126
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,180
I'm Ryotsu.

127
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:08,140
If we give our real names,

128
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:09,900
there's no point in wearing masks, is there?

129
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:10,600
That's right.

130
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:13,260
We are the Masked Brothers!

131
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:15,560
I'm number one, and this one is number two.

132
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:19,340
We don't have to appear
under our real names, do we?

133
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:21,120
Well, okay...

134
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:24,100
Yes.

135
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:26,880
One person becomes the human crane,

136
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,720
while the other operates it,

137
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:30,660
within a three-minute time limit,

138
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:32,940
grab as many prizes as you like.

139
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:35,520
However, you can only return

140
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,480
to the starting point once.

141
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:39,440
The top five pairs with the
highest total value of prizes won

142
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:41,900
advance to the final
round held right after this.

143
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:44,120
There's a final round?

144
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:45,000
Yes.

145
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:47,040
If you win the championship there,

146
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:48,300
you'll move on to the special stage,

147
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:51,520
where you can take on the human crane
challenge to grab ten-thousand-yen bills.

148
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:58,120
Now I'm getting even more motivated!

149
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:01,040
Crane ready.

150
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:03,720
I'm not very good at this sort of thing,
you know.

151
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:08,440
Don't worry, if you just move it the way I say,
everything will go smoothly.

152
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,940
Alright, Masked Brothers team, start!

153
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,900
First, please raise it up.

154
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:20,060
Stop, then move forward.

155
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:20,780
Roger.

156
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:24,902
Mm...

157
00:08:24,952 --> 00:08:28,560
Just as expected from the Kameari
Shopping District Association.

158
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:32,020
Looks like they just put
out whatever prizes they had.

159
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,840
That's the SMAP autograph

160
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,280
Stop, stop!

161
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:41,380
You found it? Nice work, Ryo.

162
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:42,720
No, it's a strawberry.

163
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:49,560
Wait, if we grab the
signed SMAP card right here,

164
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,000
Chief, I got it.

165
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:52,520
Alright, let's move it forward.

166
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:54,920
Right, back to duty.

167
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:57,020
The final round is the one
where the yen grab is biggest.

168
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,040
Let's pretend we didn't see that.

169
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:03,220
Lowering the crane!

170
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:05,060
I was mistaken.

171
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:06,740
Please move it forward.

172
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:08,160
No way.

173
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:13,060
That's the first print run of the
PlayStation version of Tokimeki Memorial.

174
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:15,320
Stop, stop, please lower it.

175
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,320
I'd given up,
thinking I could never get one now,

176
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,960
but to find one in a place like this!

177
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:25,760
That's the 1/48 series from Gendai Mokei,
out of print for twenty years.

178
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:30,160
And it's the Tiger II with the Number 13 Rommel figure,
no less!

179
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:31,840
Crane two, left, left!

180
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:37,300
Premium price, my foot! That's 100,000 yen,
and it's not even worth it!

181
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:42,120
For Brother One, all prize values are
calculated at their listed retail price.

182
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:44,880
What? So this one's only worth 500 yen?

183
00:09:45,740 --> 00:09:49,580
Damn it, we need to grab items with higher
list prices or we won't make the finals!

184
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:53,740
Forward! Right, right! Now back left!

185
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:57,080
What is that guy been
grabbing this whole time?

186
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,940
Ryo! I mean, Masked Brother One!

187
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:03,820
Our target is the signed SMAP card!
Search properly!

188
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,200
I'm searching!

189
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:08,200
That's why I'm moving out the
things that might get in the way!

190
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:11,500
It just looks like you're
picking out the expensive items.

191
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:15,940
Isn't that it over there!

192
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:20,400
What's the big idea all of a sudden?

193
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:21,940
Not "Buccho," Number Two.

194
00:10:21,940 --> 00:10:24,740
There, there's an autograph
card underneath, right?

195
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:26,360
Isn't it an autograph card from SMAP?

196
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:31,940
No, it's another idol's autograph.

197
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:37,420
That's strange, there should only
be SMAP autograph cards, though.

198
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:38,720
You, Number One!

199
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:41,080
Hey, looking closely, it was SMAP after all.

200
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:44,260
But my position's bad,
so I can't get a good shot.

201
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:46,760
Surely it'll reach.

202
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:50,080
Oh no, I missed it!

203
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:51,740
That was so obviously on purpose.

204
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:52,900
Come on, grab it!

205
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:55,540
I missed it again!

206
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:57,260
Hmph, hmph, hmph.

207
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:58,660
Hey, that ring thing...

208
00:10:58,660 --> 00:10:59,340
Oh no!

209
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:01,280
Oh no, I did it again!

210
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:05,640
Come on, this time you're sure to get it!

211
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:09,820
Excuse me, I can't hold any more.

212
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:11,800
Just throw one away, then.

213
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:13,880
How could I possibly do
something so wasteful?

214
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:16,240
Then grab it with your mouth!

215
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:17,540
Damn it, what happened?

216
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:20,680
What is this?

217
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:22,200
What are you doing?

218
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,840
Hurry up and grab that signed card!

219
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:27,460
This is a legendary classic car.

220
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:28,800
Toyota 2000GT

221
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,640
Who would've thought it'd
be in a place like this?

222
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:32,800
Forget the car!

223
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:33,800
It's a signed card!

224
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:36,680
If we grab this,
we're guaranteed to advance to the finals.

225
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:37,440
Who cares about the finals?

226
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,680
What I want is the signed card!

227
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:41,780
In that case...

228
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:46,780
That's not the right card, the card!

229
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,720
Wow, they're holding up the
car with incredible flair.

230
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:54,020
Ten seconds left!

231
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:57,640
And that's time!

232
00:11:59,540 --> 00:12:03,480
Still holding up the car, Masked Brothers No.
1 crosses the goal!

233
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:05,560
Now, the prize's retail value is...

234
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:09,860
Wow, it's 2.72 million yen,
95 yen with tax included.

235
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,980
I'm going home.

236
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:17,860
Wait, we've advanced to the final!

237
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:20,840
I only wanted the signed card.

238
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:24,140
Yet even with the card right in front of you,
you don't even try to grab it.

239
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:26,860
I really couldn't grab it, you know.

240
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:30,080
I don't want to hear your lame excuses.

241
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:32,060
After all, you only entered this game

242
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:34,780
just to exploit my fight with Hiromi,
didn't you?

243
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:37,040
Uh-oh, he's seen through it!

244
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:39,640
Come on, we're going back to duty right now.

245
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:40,660
Wait, please!

246
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:43,480
Even in the final,
we can still get the SMAP signed card!

247
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:44,380
What?

248
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:45,760
Right?

249
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:49,840
The final round prize is
actually something else...

250
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:50,260
Ugh!

251
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:52,580
What's one more prize? It won't hurt, right?

252
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:55,260
Yes! There's also a signed SMAP card!

253
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,400
This time, I'll definitely get it!

254
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:59,360
You want to make up with Hiromi, don't you!

255
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:02,780
You bastard! Taking advantage
of someone's weakness like that!

256
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,960
Well then,
let's do our best in the final too!

257
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:08,060
The Masked Brothers advance to the final!

258
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:21,960
Thank you for waiting.

259
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:27,500
We will now begin the final of the Kameari
Shopping District Association's human crane contest.

260
00:13:28,420 --> 00:13:32,220
These are the ten players, five pairs,
who fought through the preliminaries.

261
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:40,380
As expected of those
who made it to the final,

262
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:42,060
they look like tough opponents.

263
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,700
You're sure you'll really be fine this time?

264
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:45,880
Leave it to us.

265
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:47,620
We'll make sure to win.

266
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:49,520
It's a signed card!

267
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:50,620
Well, of course.

268
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:51,840
That's a SMAP autograph, right?

269
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:54,660
I haven't forgotten it for even a moment.

270
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:56,300
I'm somewhat suspicious.

271
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:58,460
Now, for this very special day,

272
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:00,400
we've invited a special guest.

273
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:05,340
It's Katsushika Police
Station Chief Tomita Kome.

274
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:06,720
Thank you, thank you.

275
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:11,340
With Chief Tomita here,
the first stage of the final

276
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:14,040
is the Underwater Piranha Stage!

277
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:21,720
A waterproofed luxury prize
has been sunk inside this tank.

278
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:24,780
However,
piranhas have been released into the tank.

279
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:28,700
If you stay underwater too long, the
piranhas will attack, so please be careful.

280
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,340
Now, let's begin.

281
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:34,360
Next up is the Atsumi Compensation Team.

282
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:38,580
I thought my heart was going to stop.

283
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,260
If the Chief shows up...

284
00:14:41,060 --> 00:14:41,780
It's fine.

285
00:14:41,780 --> 00:14:43,740
We have these masks.

286
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:45,080
There's no way we'll be found out.

287
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:47,740
But if we do get found out...

288
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:48,660
Chief

289
00:14:48,660 --> 00:14:50,840
There was a case my acquaintance handled,

290
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:54,140
where a daughter stabbed her
father over and over again.

291
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,440
The root cause was...

292
00:14:56,440 --> 00:15:00,200
the father had accidentally
used his daughter's towel.

293
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,200
No way.

294
00:15:02,220 --> 00:15:03,140
Over something as trivial as a falling-out,

295
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:04,980
that's a trifle, but it can be dangerous.

296
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:08,840
If you don't make up while you can,
you'll regret it for the rest of your life.

297
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:11,800
Instead, your hatred for each
other just keeps piling up,

298
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:15,020
and before you know it,
it could put a sudden end to your life.

299
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:17,420
Is that really okay, Chief?

300
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,420
Let's not worry about the
chief and just carry on.

301
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,240
If we're too obvious about it,
they'll sense something's up.

302
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:24,940
Got it?

303
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:26,460
A-all right, I understand.

304
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:30,380
Now, the next pair to take on
the Underwater Piranha Stage is...

305
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:37,360
Don't be nervous, or we'll be found out.

306
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:41,180
Alright, we're all set.

307
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,860
And now, let the game begin!

308
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:47,620
Forward.

309
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:49,020
Sorry, sorry.

310
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:52,160
Uh-oh.

311
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:56,200
The water's surface glare makes
it surprisingly hard to see.

312
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:58,520
I just can't stop worrying about it.

313
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:00,580
Number 2, a bit more to the right, right!

314
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:15,800
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

315
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,640
Terrifying, Masked Brother Number 1.

316
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,600
I'm not worried about the piranhas at all.

317
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:25,600
We've drifted away from the planned spot.

318
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:27,020
There's nothing worth taking here.

319
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:29,100
If it comes to this,
we're going to win this match.

320
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:37,340
That one...

321
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:41,240
That's right, that's right.

322
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:43,880
Why aren't you grabbing it?

323
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:45,280
There's no way you didn't notice!

324
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:45,840
Hup!

325
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:50,160
Not "hmm," Number One!

326
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:52,680
And that's time!

327
00:16:55,200 --> 00:17:01,060
And the total value of the prizes won is 128,721 yen,
tax included.

328
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:02,460
Narrowly dropping to second place.

329
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:05,620
Wait, there's this one too!

330
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:06,760
What?!

331
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:08,680
It's definitely shifted!

332
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:12,620
Sorry about that.
Our team has been announced at the top.

333
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:14,020
Of course.

334
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:17,420
Why didn't you grab the signed card?

335
00:17:17,420 --> 00:17:19,780
It was right in front of you!

336
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:22,140
I didn't notice.

337
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,880
Don't play dumb.

338
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,960
After all, we don't have oxygen tanks.

339
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:30,240
We didn't have time to size up the prizes.

340
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:34,760
Well, let's talk about that later.

341
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:36,880
Hey, you two.

342
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:42,880
Don't tell me they saw us.

343
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:45,680
Idiot!

344
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:49,460
Move it exactly like I told you!
Don't let it get away!

345
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:51,380
What do you think you're doing?!

346
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:54,500
This is the only way to
clear the Chief's suspicions.

347
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:58,060
Even if they've got a hunch
about who we really are,

348
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:01,180
They'd never expect me
to hit the Chief, right?

349
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:03,460
That may be true, but...

350
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:06,140
Our goal is to win, isn't it?

351
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:08,180
Don't let your guard down for a second.

352
00:18:08,180 --> 00:18:09,640
Sorry, sorry.

353
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,260
Sorry isn't good enough!

354
00:18:10,820 --> 00:18:12,580
There's no need to go all out, is there?

355
00:18:14,020 --> 00:18:15,340
Then won't the Chief find out?

356
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:16,960
If we get caught, we're fired! Fired!

357
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:19,120
There'll be no promotions or bonuses either.

358
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:20,260
Do you understand?

359
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:22,780
Yes, yes, I understand.

360
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:24,080
Good. As long as you understand.

361
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:25,760
Make sure you do it properly from now on.

362
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:29,580
W-what an intimidating presence!

363
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:32,140
I was going to point out the piranha
still clinging to your backside

364
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:33,340
but...

365
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:36,440
There was no way we could speak up.
The atmosphere was too intense.

366
00:18:37,540 --> 00:18:40,240
And now, the final stage!

367
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:41,680
The current leader is

368
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:47,280
the Masked Brothers team with 3,975,527 yen,
tax included.

369
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:50,320
And the winning team will

370
00:18:50,660 --> 00:18:54,380
take on the 10,000-yen
grab human crane challenge.

371
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:57,200
The championship is ours.

372
00:18:58,060 --> 00:19:00,160
I can't trust this guy anymore.

373
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:03,000
This is it!

374
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:12,200
Oh, you're right!

375
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:14,720
If the Chief finds out,
we're in big trouble.

376
00:19:15,060 --> 00:19:18,680
Promotions might not matter to you,
but there won't be any bonuses.

377
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:19,660
I'm just going to go take a look!

378
00:19:25,980 --> 00:19:27,120
You're late, Ichigo.

379
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:28,940
You set me up, didn't you!

380
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:31,640
Come on, come on, get into position quickly.

381
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:32,940
W-wait a second.

382
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:37,960
I'm definitely going to
get that SMAP signed card.

383
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:44,560
The final stage of the championship is
the Balloon Bomb Battle Royale stage.

384
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:47,600
Bombs are hidden inside the balloons,

385
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:49,740
and they explode when touched.

386
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:53,240
Bombs, you say? Isn't it that kind
that just releases white powder?

387
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:55,720
The kind you often see on
TV variety shows, right?

388
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:58,100
And now, please take a look at this.

389
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,740
After winning the life-or-death battle,

390
00:20:02,740 --> 00:20:07,660
which team will actually get to
attempt the 10,000-yen grab challenge?

391
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:13,440
Final stage, start!

392
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:18,480
What's wrong, Ichiro?
Why aren't you moving it?

393
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:20,540
Number Two, I can't do it. Let's switch.

394
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:23,500
I can grab a signed SMAP card at least.

395
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,560
I'm saying winning is impossible.

396
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:27,900
Stop your yapping and just move it already.

397
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:29,040
Absolutely not.

398
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:31,580
If you refuse to move it no matter what,

399
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:33,920
What?

400
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:37,200
How pushy of you!

401
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:38,600
You're the Mask!

402
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:41,720
It's for the bond between
a father and his daughter!

403
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:43,800
Sorry, but you're going
to have to cooperate!

404
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:44,820
That's dirty!

405
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:46,960
Take your hand off that
and come back right away!

406
00:20:47,380 --> 00:20:49,300
Once we've got the autographed card,
all right!

407
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:51,040
You're so stubborn!

408
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:52,760
In that case, this is what I'll do!

409
00:20:53,760 --> 00:20:54,560
Stop it!

410
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:56,720
Rigo, switch places with me!

411
00:20:56,780 --> 00:20:59,000
This time I'll definitely
get the autographed card too!

412
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:01,340
How could I trust someone like you!

413
00:21:01,520 --> 00:21:02,180
Ahead! Ahead!

414
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:08,060
That's bad for the heart.

415
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:11,100
What are you

416
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:16,280
What a tenacious guy!

417
00:21:16,280 --> 00:21:19,260
You're unlucky, give up.

418
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:21,020
I won't take orders from you.

419
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:23,900
Where are the latest instructions?

420
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:25,740
Stop being so stupid.

421
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,600
Don't get in my way.

422
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:30,400
Aaaaah!

423
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:31,860
Aaaaah!

424
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:32,860
Aaaaah!

425
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:36,440
All sorts of...

426
00:21:38,020 --> 00:21:39,660
Eeeeeh!

427
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:42,940
Aaaaah!

428
00:21:43,560 --> 00:21:44,880
Then, aaaah!

429
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:56,740
Where's Tsumappi's autographed card?

430
00:21:58,680 --> 00:21:59,780
Whoa!

431
00:22:02,760 --> 00:22:05,780
We did it! Now I'm making up with Hiromi.

432
00:22:08,820 --> 00:22:11,000
Well, that's... no way, what do you mean?!

433
00:22:13,660 --> 00:22:15,400
Everybody, please take notice!

434
00:22:25,740 --> 00:22:27,720
Dokidoki Memorial,

435
00:22:27,770 --> 00:22:29,800
the Toyota 2000GT...

436
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:33,520
Too bad, Masked Brothers Number One.

437
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:36,780
No, Ryotsu Kankichi-kun.

438
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:39,660
C-Chief...

439
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:42,920
Looks like you went all out again this time.

440
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:44,600
Not really.

441
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:49,440
I have good news and bad news.
Which would you like to hear first?

442
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,820
Th-then, the bad news first.

443
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:53,960
You've got some nerve.

444
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:58,940
Ryotsu-kun, you're going to pay for
all the damages this time, got it?

445
00:22:58,940 --> 00:23:01,280
What?! This was all Number Two's doing!

446
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:03,640
No, it's Chief Ohara's fault!

447
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:06,940
The Chief goes wild,
and this is what happens!

448
00:23:08,540 --> 00:23:10,590
Autograph, autograph,

449
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:12,740
the SMAP autograph.

450
00:23:12,740 --> 00:23:15,880
Where's the making up with your daughter?
Where is it?

451
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:17,836
That's...

452
00:23:17,886 --> 00:23:20,620
the SMAP autograph.

453
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:25,080
The SMAP signature for
making up with my daughter.

454
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:26,680
Hey, look, that's Chief Ohara, isn't it?

455
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:29,660
No, it must just be a
stranger who looks like him.

456
00:23:29,660 --> 00:23:33,320
A serious man like Ohara
wouldn't be in a place like this.

457
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:34,980
Yes, there's no doubt about it.

458
00:23:35,660 --> 00:23:36,060
No way.

459
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:38,740
Chief, what about the good news?

460
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:42,720
You don't have to work anymore, Ryotsu.

461
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:44,000
You're fired.

462
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,220
Fired?

463
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:48,420
Then at least let me
cut off a finger properly.

464
00:23:48,420 --> 00:23:50,560
This job is essential.

465
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:53,540
I won't listen. Figure it out yourself.

466
00:23:53,540 --> 00:23:56,240
Chief, that's awful.

467
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:57,420
As a human being,

468
00:24:03,740 --> 00:24:06,720
Nakagawa,
what do you mean you're quitting the police?

469
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:08,840
My old man decided it all on his own.

470
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:11,940
Don't joke around.
It's a job you chose yourself.

471
00:24:11,940 --> 00:24:14,160
Are you going to abandon
your manly ambitions?

472
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:17,360
I'd be in trouble without you, too.

473
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:21,840
Next time:
"Fierce President Nakagawa's Father." See you then!

474
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:38,860
Yaaah!

475
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:40,160
No, no!

476
00:24:40,540 --> 00:24:41,820
Please, please!

477
00:24:42,280 --> 00:24:43,280
Whoa!

478
00:24:44,420 --> 00:24:46,240
Well then, right there

479
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,520
So, yeah!

480
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:50,440
Yaaah!

481
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:51,920
Debe-debe!

482
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:53,320
Flustered!

483
00:24:53,500 --> 00:24:54,460
No, no!

484
00:24:54,840 --> 00:25:00,080
Yaaah!

485
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:02,860
Everyone, gather!

486
00:25:03,500 --> 00:25:06,300
If you come here,

487
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:12,640
a dreamlike final energy

488
00:25:13,820 --> 00:25:17,100
gaze at tomorrow and believe in yesterday,

489
00:25:17,100 --> 00:25:20,040
draw the universe and
stand firm on the earth,

490
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:23,740
Kameari's star is coming,
what a strange thing, oh yeah!

491
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:27,500
This should be fine, right?

492
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:28,980
No way that's fine!

493
00:25:38,680 --> 00:25:42,440
Thank you for watching.

